<mujoco model="xarm6_pusht_tabletop_tee_start">
  <!-- The four T-block scenes' shared starting pose, read generically by
       oim/runtime/mjcf.py (it looks for a keyframe named "start" and falls
       back to its own clutter-tuned constant otherwise).

       Its own file, not common.xml's, because icra_sign includes common.xml
       too and pushes a different object from a different pose -- and not
       tee.xml's, because the "_point" twins include tee.xml and declare
       their own keyframe over the pusher's joints instead.

       qpos is arm joints 1-5, then the block's SE(2) start pose, then its
       vertical DoF. Angles here are radians: <compiler angle="degree"> (from
       ../xarm6/xarm6.xml) converts angle-valued *attributes*, not keyframe
       qpos.

       The five joint values are the standard forward-facing work pose,
       [0, -45, -45, 0, 90] deg: the arm reaches out over the middle of the
       table with the stick pointing straight down (0.0 deg off vertical),
       tip at (0.255, 0, 0.323) -- centred in y, 0.32 m above the surface
       and 0.43 m from the block, so ADMM has to drive the arm out to first
       contact the way a real deployment would.

       It replaces the lab's own home pose, which put the tip at
       (0.381, 0.440) -- 4 cm from the block's start, i.e. already parked
       against it before the first plan. ../xarm6_pusht_tabletop_real/
       keeps the lab pose, since that is where the real arm actually homes.

       The block's vertical DoF is 0: its body sits at the geoms' own
       half-height (0.0298), so at T_zs = 0 the bottom face is exactly on the
       table top and it starts resting.

       tests/test_scenes.py re-checks, per scene, that this pose starts clear
       of every obstacle, tip-down, above the table and not already on the
       object -- a shared pose has to work in all four, and one tuned against
       single_obstacle alone once started 3.7 cm *inside* shelf_gap's
       shelf_2. -->
  <keyframe>
    <key name="start"
      qpos="0.0 -0.785 -0.785 0.0 1.5708 0.381 0.400 0.0 0.0"/>
  </keyframe>
</mujoco>
